<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Fier</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Fier is a city in south-western Albania, near the ruins of the ancient Greek city of Apollonia. It grew from a 19th-century market town and became a centre of oil and chemical industry under communism. In 1935 it was the centre of an armed revolt against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zog-i">King Zog</a>, which was quickly suppressed.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/fier.jpg" alt="Fier" width="320" height="231" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Sharon Hahn Darlin · CC BY 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Fier,_Albania_2022-11-03_-_Trees_along_street.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
